rational: things that I want to achieve and are maybe unusual/special

  simple functional langauge (FUN) (statically typed) for low level (OS) programming
  FUN looks like ocaml (syntactic subset) allowing easy piggy back on Ocaml dev/type-checker
  own (AoT) compiler for FUN (coded in Haskell)
  compiler dev by pipeline of stages, each with own interpreter/evaluator to help ensure semantic correctness
  by default: agressive optimization of FUN (inlining and constant folding/propogation) via normalization (NbE)
  but with inlining control in user program
  target baremetal x86 (stretch: maybe 6502 also!)
  (very) non standard ABI and runtime model
  no use of stack by user programs (they will be fully CPSed)
  continuations are allocated in the heap like any other datastructure
  all memory will be allocated in Garbage collected heap.
  garbage collector implemented at the OS level (rather like a VM)
  idea: use of x86 stack pointer for heap allocation

  simple/cheap co-operative concurrency (fibers) -- one of the drivers to have no stack in user code

  big stretch: GC algorithm implemented in user code
  basic round robin fiber scheduler
  stretch: scheduler for fibers in user space
